    "rs|RS224_2011-12-22|floor": "Vol. 224 Thursday \nNo. 21 22 December, 2011 \n 1 Pausa, 1933 (Saka) \n \n  \nPARLIAMENTARY DEBATES \nRAJYA SABHA \nOFFICIAL REPORT \nCONTENTS \nPapers Laid on the Table (page 1-19) \nMessages from Lok Sabha– \n Export-Import Bank of India (Amendment) Bill, 2011 -  Reported (page \n20) \n Factoring Regulation Bill, 2011- Laid on the Table (page 60) \nReport of the Department Related Parliamentary Standing Committee on Home \nAffairs – Laid on the Table (page 20) \nReports of the Committee on Empowerment of Women -  Laid on the Table \n(page 20) \nReport of the Department Related Parliamentary Standing Committee on \nEnergy - Laid on the Table (pages 20-21) \nReports of the Department Related Parliamentary Standing Committee on \nFinance - Laid on the Table (page 21) \nReport of the Department Related Parliamentary Standing Committee on \nFood, Consumer Affairs and Public Distribution -  Laid on the Table (page \n21) \nReports of the Department Related Parliamentary Standing Committee on \nInformation Technology - Laid on the Table (page 22) \nReports of the Department Related Parliamentary Standing Committee on \nPetroleum and Natural Gas - Laid on the Table (pages 22-23) \n[P.T.O.\n \n© \nRAJYA SABHA SECRETARIAT \nNEW DELHI \n\n\nPRICE : Rs. 50.00 \n\nReport of the Department Related Parliamentary Standing Committee on \nSocial Justice and Empowerment - Laid on the Table (pages 23)  \nStatement of the Department Related Parliamentary Standing Committee on \nExternal Affairs -Laid on the Table (page 23) \nGovernment Bills– \n The National Commission for Human Resources for Health Bill, 2011 -  \nIntroduced (page 23) \n The Constitution (Scheduled Tribes) Order (Amendment) Bill, 2011 -  \nPassed (pages 23-45) \n The Appropriation Railways (No.3) Bill, 2011 -  Returned (pages 45-\n125) \n The Railway Property (Unlawful Possession) Amendment Bill, 2008 -  \nPassed (pages 45-125) \n The New Delhi Municipal Council (Amendment) Bill, 2011 -  Passed \n(pages 125-139) \nMotion for Constitution of a Joint Committee for Welfare of Other \nBackward Classes (OBCs) - Adopted (pages 139-140) \n \n \n \n \n \n \nWeb-site Address : http://rajyasabha.nic.in \n\n  http://parliamentofindia.nic.in \nE-mail Address : rsedit-e@sansad.nic.in \n\n \nPUBLISHED UNDER RULE 260 OF RULES OF PROCEDURE AND CONDUCT OF BUSINESS  \nIN THE COUNCIL OF STATES (RAJYA SABHA) AND PRINTED BY SUNLIGHT PRINTERS,  \nE1/16, ANSARI ROAD, DARYAGANJ, DELHI-110002 \n \n\n 1 \nRAJYA SABHA \nThursday, the 22nd December, 2011/1 Pausa, 1933 (Saka) \nThe House met at eleven of the clock, \nMR. DEPUTY CHAIRMAN in the Chair. \nPAPERS LAID ON THE TABLE \nI. Report and Accounts (2010-11) of Coir Board, Kochi and related Papers \nII. Report and Accounts (2010- 11) of CGTMSE, Mumbai, MGIRI, Wardha and \nrelated papers \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF PARLIAMENTARY AFFAIRS (SHRI \nRAJEEV SHUKLA) : Sir, I, on behalf of Shri Virbhadra Singh, lay on the \nTable– \nI. A copy each (in English and Hindi) of the following papers under \nSection  \n  19 and sub-section (4) of Section 17 of the Coir -Industry Act, \n1953:- \n (a) Fifty-seventh Annual Report of the Coir Board, Kochi, for \nthe year 2010-11. \n (b) Annual Accounts of the Coir Board, Kochi, for the year \n2010-11. and the Audit Report thereon. \n (c) Statement by Government accepting the Annual Report of the \nabove Board. \n (d) Statement by Government accepting the Annual Accounts and \nAudit Report of the above Board. \nII. A copy each (in English and Hindi) of the following papers:- \n(i) (a) Eleventh Annual Report and Accounts of the Credit \nGuarantee Fund Trust for Micro and Small Enterprises \n(CGTMSE), Mumbai, for the year 2010- 11, together with the \nAuditor’s Report on the Accounts. \n (b) Statement by Government accepting the above Report. \n(ii) (a) Annual Report and Accounts of the Mahatma Gandhi Institute \nfor Rural Industrialization (MGIRI), Wardha for the year \n2010-11, together with the Auditor’s Report on the \nAccounts. \n\n 2 \n (b) Statement by Government accepting the above Report. \n\n 3 \nReport and Accounts (2010-11) of various Institutes  \nand Council and related Papers. \nTHE MINISTER OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE (SHRI GHULAM NABI AZAD) : \nSir, I lay on the Table, a copy each (in English and Hindi) of the \nfollowing papers:— \n (i) (a) Annual Report and Accounts of the Pasteur Institute of \nIndia, Coonoor. for the year 2010- 11, together with the \nAuditor’s Report on the Accounts. \n  (b) Review by Government on the working of the above Institute. \n (ii) (a) Annual Report and Accounts of the National Institute of \nBiologicals, Noida, for the year 2010-11, together with the \nAuditor’s Report on the Accounts. \n  (b) Review by Government on the working of the above Institute. \n (iii) (a) Annual Report and Accounts of the Pharmacy Council of \nIndia, New Delhi, for the year 2010- 11, together with the \nAuditor’s Report on the Accounts. \n (b) Review by Government on the working of the above Council. \nI. Report (2010-11) of Cochin Port Trust Cochin and related papers \nII. Report and Accounts (2010-11) of Indian Maritime University, Chennai \nand related papers. \nSHRI RAJEEV SHUKLA : Sir, I, on behalf of Shri G.K. Vasan, lay on the \nTable— \n I. A copy each (in English and Hindi) of the following papers, \nunder Section 106 of the Major Port Trusts Act, 1963:— \n  (a) Administration Report of the Cochin Port Trust, Cochin, for \nthe year 2010-11. \n  (b) Review by Government on the working of the above Port \nTrust. \n II. A copy each (in English and Hindi) of the following papers:- \n  (a) Second Annual Report of the Indian Maritime University, \nChennai, for the year 2010- 11 together with the Auditor’s \nReport on the Accounts. \n\n 4 \n  (b) Annual Accounts of the Indian Maritime University, Chennai, \nfor the year 2010-11, and the Audit Report thereon. \n  (c) Review by Government on the working of the above \nUniversity. \nReport and Accounts (2010-11) of various companies and related papers \nSHRI RAJEEV SHUKLA : Sir, I, on behalf of Shri Praful Patel, lay on \nthe Table, under sub- section (1) of Section 619A of the Companies Act, \n1956, a copy each (in English and Hindi) of the following papers: \n (i) (a) Sixty-fourth Annual Report and Accounts of  the Nepa \nLimited, Nepanagar, Madhya Pradesh, for the year 2010- 11, \ntogether with the Auditor’s Report on the Accounts and the \ncomments of the Comptroller and Auditor General of India \nthereon. \n  (b) Review by Government on the working of the above Company. \n (ii) (a) Forty-first Annual Report and Accounts of the Hindustan \nPaper Corporation Limited, Kolkata, for the year 2010- 11, \ntogether with the Auditor’s Report on the Accounts and the \ncomments of the Comptroller and Auditor General of India \nthereon. \n  (b) Review by Government on the working of the above \nCorporation, \n (iii) (a) Forty-first Annual Report and Accounts of the \nEngineering Projects (India) Limited (EPI), New Delhi, for \nthe year 2010-11, together with the Auditor’s Report on the \nAccounts and the comments of the Comptroller and Auditor \nGeneral of India thereon. \n (b) Statement by Government accepting the above Report. \nReports and Accounts (2010-11) of various Institutes and related papers  \nSHRI RAJEEV SHUKLA : Sir, I, on behalf of Shri Dinsha J. Patel, lay \non the Table, a copy each (in English and Hindi) of the following papers \n:— \n  (i) (a) Annual Report and Accounts of the National Institute of \nRock Mechanics (NIRM), Kolar, Karnataka, for the year 2010-\n11, together with the Auditor’s Report on the Accounts. \n\n 5 \n (b) Review by Government on the working of the above Institute. \n\n 6 \n (ii) (a) Annual Report and Accounts of the National Institute of \nMiners’ Health, Nagpur, for the year 2010-11, together with \nthe Auditor’s Report on the Accounts. \n (c) Review by Government on the working of the above institute. \nReport and Accounts (2010-11) of LNUPE, Gwalior and related Papers \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE OF THE MINISTRY OF YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS \n(SHRI AJAY MAKEN) : Sir, I lay on the Table, a copy each (in English and \nHindi) of the following papers:— \n (a) Annual Report and Accounts of the Lakshmibai National University \nof Physical Eucation (LNUPE), Gwalior, for the year 2010- 11, \ntogether with the Auditor’s Report on the Accounts. \n(b) Review by Government on the working of the above University. \nReports and Accounts (2010-11) of NERAMAC, Guwahati and related Papers \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE OF THE MINISTRY OF DEVELOPMENT OF NORTH EASTERN \nREGION AND MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF PARLIAMENTARY AFFAIRS \n(SHRI PABAN SINGH GHATOWAR) : Sir, I lay on the Table, under sub- section \n(1) of Section 619A of the Companies Act, 1956, a copy each (in English \nand Hindi) of the following papers : – \n(a) Twenty-ninth Annual Report and Accounts of the North Eastern \nRegional Agricultural Marketing Corporation Limited (NERAMAC), \nGuwahati, for the year 2010- 11, together with the Auditor’s \nReport on the Accounts and the comments of the Comptroller and \nAuditor General of India thereon. \n(b) Statement by Government accepting the above Report. \nReport and Accounts (2010-11) of ICWA, New Delhi, RIS,  \nNew Delhi and related papers \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS AND THE \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT (SHRI E. \nAHAMED) : Sir, I lay on the Table, a copy each (in English and Hindi) of \nthe following papers :- \n\n 7 \n (i) (a) Annual Report of the Indian Council of World Affairs \n(ICWA), New Delhi, for the year 2010-11. \n  (b) Annual Accounts of the Indian Council of World Affairs \n(ICWA), New Delhi, for the year 2010- 11 and the Audit \nReport thereon. \n  (c) Statement by Government accepting the above Reports. \n  (ii) (a) Annual Report and Accounts of the Research and \nInformation System for Developing Countries (RIS), New \nDelhi, for the year 2010- 11, together with the Auditor’s \nReport on the Accounts. \n (b) Review by Government on the working of the above \nOrganization. \nI. Notification of the Ministry of Personnel, Public Grievances and \nPensions \nII. Report and Accounts (2010- 11) of various central organizations and \nrelated papers. \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \n(SHRI D. PURANDESWARI) : Sir, I, on behalf of Shri V. Narayanasamy, lay \non the Table— \n I.  A copy (in English and Hindi) of the Ministry of Personnel, \nPublic Grievances and Pensions (Department of Personnel and \nTraining) Notification No. G.S.R. 660 (E), dated the 3rd \nSeptember, 2011, publishing the Indian Police Service \n(Recruitment) Amendment Rules, 2011, under sub- section (2) of \nSection 3 of the All India Services Act, 1951. \n II.  A copy each (in English and Hindi) of the following papers: - \n  (i) (a) Annual Report and Accounts of the Central Civil \nServices Cultural and Sports Board, New Delhi, for the \nyear 2010-11, together with the Auditor’s Report on \nthe Accounts. \n   (b) Statement by Government accepting the above Report. \n   (ii) (a) Annual Report and Accounts of the Kendriya \nBhandar, New Delhi, for the year 2010- 11, together \nwith the Auditor’s Report on the Accounts. \n\n 8 \n   (b) Review by Government on the working of the above \nOrganization. \n\n 9 \n  (iii) (a) Annual Report and Accounts of the Civil Services \nSociety (Sanskrit School) (CSS), New Delhi, for the \nyear 2010-11, together with the Auditor’s Report on \nthe Accounts. \n  (b) Statement by Government accepting the above report. \n  (iv) (a) Annual Report and Accounts of the North Eastern Space \nApplications Centre (NE- SAC). Umiam, Meghalaya, for \nthe year 2010- 11, together with the Auditor’s Report \non the Accounts. \n   (b) Statement by Government accepting the above Report. \nReport and Accounts 2008-09, 2009-10, (