जाते ह�, बैठते ह�, तो पता चलता है �क वहां पर शौचालय क� क्या हालत \nहै। \n THE VICE-CHAIRMAN (PROF. P.J. KURIEN) : Please cooperate.  \n श्री प्रभात झा : वहाँ खाना कै स ा �मलता है, य�द आप यह सब दे ख�गे तो मुझे लगता है तो रे ल \nमंत्रालय, िजस पर पूर� तरह से �वश्वास हुआ करता था, उस पर कोई �वश्वास नह�ं करे गा। आज आदमी \nरे ल म� चढ़ते समय कं प कं प ा त ा है, उ स के पांव कांपते ह� चढूं या नह�ं चढूं। पैसा दे कर मौत को �नमंत्रण \nदे ने का नाम है-रे ल मंत्रालय। रे ल मंत्री जी, आप ध्यान द�िजए, आपने रे ल मंत्री बनने के बाद घोषणा \nक� थी हर स्टे ट म� जाऊ ं गा। म� आपसे अपने स्टे ट क� �डमांड नह�ं कर रहा हूं ...(व्यवधान)... \n THE VICE- CHAIRMAN (PROF. P.J. KURIEN) : Now please conclude. \nPrabhatji.  \n श्री प्रभात झा : म� अपने स्टे ट क� बात नह�ं कर रहा हूं �क यह �दया जाए। म� इतना कहकर \nअपनी बात समाप्त करता हूं। धन्यवाद। \n THE VICE-CHAIRMAN (PROF. P.J. KURIEN) : There are five speakers from \nyour party. That is the point. Thank you. Shri Rama Chandra Khuntia.  \nSHRI RAMA CHANDRA KHUNTIA (Odisha) : Sir, I rise to support the \nAppropriation Railways (No.3) Bill, 2011 and the Railway Properly \n(Unlawful Possession) Amendment Bill, 2008. While supporting these Bills, \nI also appreciate the efforts of the present Minister, who has just taken \nover as the Railway Minister, the ex-Railway Ministers, Mamata Banerjeeji \nand Lalu Prasadji of the UPA Government, our Prime Minister, Dr. Manmohan \nSingh, and our leader, Soniaji, in managing the Railways, which is the \nsecond biggest carrier in the world, without increasing the passenger \nfare from 2004 to 2011. With all its difficulties, if you look at the \ntotal earning of the Railways, it was Rs.71,605 Crores in 2007- 08 and \nRs.79,837 crores in 2008- 09. Rs.1,06,039 crores in 2011- 12. The growth \nrate was 11.4 per cent in 2008-09 and 9.1 per cent in 2009-10. it was, of \ncourse, less in 2010- 11, that is, 8.5 per cent. In 2011- 12, it is 12.2 \nper cent. The operating rate, which was 75.9 per cent in 2007- 08, has \nbeen increased to 91.11 per cent in 2011- 12. This is the performance of \nthe Railways. It is doing well. As the hon. Member said earlier, the \nappropriation which, in the year 2005- 06, was Rs. 15,440 crores and the \nclosing balance was Rs. 9,981 crores, in 2010- 11, has come down to minus \nRs. 1,975 crores, as closing balance. This is balance has gone down \n\n 85 \nbecause of the ongoing activities. Anyhow, passenger earning alone has \nincreased by 9.6 per cent to Rs. 26,007.87 crores in  \n\n 86 \n2010-11, against Rs. 23,743.63 crores in 2009, without increasing any \nfare and despite announcements of various new concessions, new projects \nand other programmes. Further, the total traffic earning has also \nincreased by 8.76 per cent, from Rs. 87,000 crores in 2009- 10 to Rs. \n94,742 crores in 2010- 11. Also the internal resource exoneration of the \nMinistry of Railways has increased by 7.7 per cent from Rs. 2,280 crores \nin 2009-10 to Rs. 9,864 crores in 2010- 11 and further it is estimated to \nincrease to Rs. 12,318 crores. Sir, in a nutshell, this is the \nperformance of the Railways. It is definitely very good. They are doing a \ngood job. If we look at the things which are happening in the Railways, I \nwould also like to give some data. From time to time, various projects \nare being announced by the Minister and then many projects have been \nstarted without plan approval. As a result of which many projects have \ncompiled. The answer has been given by the Railway Department which says \nthat for completing or doubling a new line and, new rail lines requires \naround Rs. 1,25,000 crores. This is what the Railway Department has said \nin an answer to my question. If we take all the projects, I have been \ntold that it requires Rs. 3.5 lakh crores to complete the railway \nprojects which are going on. \nSir, I want to draw your kind attention to one report of the CAG. In \nthe audit findings, 2011, No. 34, they have said very clearly, “ Audit \nexamination of 50 ongoing projects of new fines sanctioned on socio-\neconomic development of backward regions reveals that five projects \nsanctioned more than 20 years ago; nine projects sanctioned between 15 \nand 20 years ago; 36 projects sanctioned between 10 and 11 years ago, \nwere still lying incomplete as of 31st March, 2010. The progress of works \nbeing very slow, 18 of them were not expected to be completed within next \nten years. The Railway has already incurred an expenditure of Rs. 8,549 \ncrores on the 50 new line projects and the balance funds required to \ncomplete these projects were of the order of Rs. 16,800 crores.”  My \ncontention is, if you take this point, more than worth Rs. 1.5 lakh \ncrores of various projects, all over the country, are still lying which \nare not expected to be completed in 15 to 20 years. That means, the \nRailways is carrying the biggest non- performing assets, which are more \nthan those of the banks. The amount of Rs. 1.5 lakh crores, which has \nbeen spent and which is not performinq, is more than the non- performing \nassets of the banks. The question is; should the Government complete \n\n 87 \nthese projects by giving a lump sum grant for infrastructure development \nto make it perform? Otherwise, the money which has been spent and which \nis not performing, is a wastage. I think the Government has to take a \nfinal decision. The Government should give one time grant to the \nRailways. It is very important. The Government should take an appropriate \ndecision in this regard as to how to complete these ongoing projects. \nWhile declaring new projects, the Government should be very cautious. \nSir, now, I would  \n\n 88 \nlike to point out two or three aspects for the consideration of the hon. \nMinister. Firstly, there are some deviations in the Appropriation Fund. \nWe have seen, in the Railway Convention Committee, many projects being \ndeviated, and the Budget Appropriation being changed by the Zonal Office \nand the Board. When we ask for it, they give a reply saying that the \nZonal Office has the power to appropriate up to Rs.5 crores and the Board \nhas the power to appropriate up to Rs. 10 crores. I fail to understand \nhow the Appropriation, done by Parliament, can be changed by the Board \nand by the Zone by a written order. It is quite surprising, and I would \nrequest the dynamic Railway Minister to look into it and find out how the \nRailway Board and the Zonal Office, as also the Divisional Office, have \nthe power to re-appropriate; they are using the word ‘appropriation'. How \ncan they do it? I think this is totally illegal, and I would draw the \nattention of the hon. Minister to this aspect. \nSecondly, Sir, there is a notification about appointment of disabled \npersons in the Railways; that is, three per cent appointments are to be \nmade in the Railways from this category. I can say for sure that there is \nno such three per cent appointment in the Railways, and this, I would \nsay, particularly, of Odisha, where an interview was held three years \nback, and some people were selected. But, till now, in spite of repeated \nreference by the M.Ps and everybody, these people are not being \nappointed. The second aspect to which I would draw the kind attention of \nthe hon. Minister is regarding appointments for filling up vacant posts; \nthere are more than 1.7 lakh posts vacant. The Railway Board had assured \nthat they would fill up these posts within a limited period, and they \nalso started the interview process. Here, I would like to mention about a \ncircular which indicated that 10 per cent of posts in the safety category \nand 2 per cent of posts in the general category could be filled up by the \nG.Ms. Now, these posts can be filled up by the G.Ms without calling for \nan interview, and ultimately, those workers will be regularized. It only \nmeans that we are legalizing an illegal thing. Nobody in this country has \nthe power to make an appointment without an interview in government or \ncpsu and say that after four or five months these people will be \nregularized, because then, the Union people will also demand that these \npeople should also be regularized. I would like to know from the hon. \nMinister whether giving power to G.Ms, to fill up ten per cent of vacant \nposts in safety category and two per cent of vacant posts in general \n\n 89 \ncategory, is a legal thing, and whether it has the approval  \n\n 90 \nof the Government and Parliament. I am sure that there is no law in this \ncountry which says that without the approval of Parliament, such a power \ncan be given.  \nThen, Sir, I want to draw the attention of the hon. Minister to \ncompensation money given to accident victims. I am thankful to the hon. \nMinister that they are giving the compensation. But I would like to know \nwhether we can formulate a rule so as to ensure that the compensation \namount paid to victims at the time of accidents, that is, compensation \ngiven to the injured as well as the kith and kin of the deceased persons, \nmust be uniform in all cases. It cannot be Rs.2 lakhs in some cases, Rs.5 \nlakhs in some cases, and so on. So, this amount should be made uniform \neverywhere. \nSir, then, the question of the ZRUCC, I am sorry to inform...  \nTHE VICE-CHAIRMAN (PROF. P.J. KURIEN): Please conclude.  \nSHRI RAMA CHANDRA KHUNTIA: This is not regularly meeting. \nThen, Sir, I want to draw the kind attention of the hon. Minister to \nthe deputation process. Now, it is a fact that many people are working on \ndeputation in the Railways. I want to knew how many persons in the \nRailways are working on deputation in various Corporations and other \nbodies, and getting the deputation allowance over and above their pay, \nwhich is also adding to the expenditure of the Railways. \nBefore I conclude, I just want to bring to the attention of the hon. \nMinister some demands pertaining to my State. I have been demanding for a \nsurvey of the gagpur Keonjhar Road to gagpur Railway line. Then, we have \nalso given a proposal for three rail lines, namely, Rupsa- Burhamara to \nChakulia (35 kms), Nuapada- Gunupur B.G. rail link to Theravali (75 kms) \nand Banspani- Badabil rail link, and also for the setting up of the \nrailway wagon factory at Ganjam and Kalahandi. Sir, then, the State \nGovernment of Odisha has given proposals for introduction of Puri Mumbai \nDuronto Express, Puri Jaipur- Jodhpur-Duronto Express. Puri Pune- Duronto \nExpress, Bhubaneswar- Bangalore Express. Bhubaneswar- Surat Express, \nSuperfast Express train from Visakhapatnam to Prayag (Allahabad) via \nBhubaneswar...  \nTHE VICE-CHAIRMAN (PROF. P. J. KURIEN): Okay, okay.  \nSHRI RAMA CHANDRA KHUNTIA: Just one minute, Sir. (Interruptions) \n\n 91 \nThere are proposals for railway projects’ given by the State Government, \nnamely, Meramandali-Angul-Talcher- \n\n 92 \nChhendipada Dedicated Industrial Rail Corridor, Bharchuna- Haridaspur-\nParadip Road, the Khurda -Bolangir Road, Rupsa-Bangriposi Road and Khurda \nRoad-Rajatgarh Road. All these proposals given by the Odisha Government \nmay be taken into consideration for the development of a backward State \nlike Odisha. \nश्री वीर �स ंह (उत्तर प्रदे श) : मान्यवर. आपने मुझे इन दोन� �वधेयक� पर बोलने का जो शुभ \nअवसर �दया है, इ स के �लए म� आपका धन्यवाद अदा करता हूँ। ये दोनो �बल्स, �व�नयोग रे ल (संख्यांक \n3) �वधेयक, 2011 तथा रे ल सम्प�त (�व�ध�वरुद्ध कब्जा) संशोधन �वधेयक, 2008 बहुत ह� महत्वपूणर् \nह�। \nमान्यवर, �व�नयोग �वधेयक द्वारा भारत क� सं�चत �न�ध म� से अनुसूची म� उिल्ल�खत रा�शय� \nसे, िजनका योग एक \nलाख रुपए होता है, �व�भन्न सेवाओं, जैसे पूंजी, रे ल �न�धयाँ व रे ल सुर�ा �न�ध \nके प्रभार� को चुकाने के बाबत �वत्त वषर् 2011-2012 के �लए द� और आयोिजत क� जा स के ग ी । दूसरा \n�वधेयक रे ल सम्पित्त �व�ध�वरुद्ध कब्जे और चोर� के अपराध� से संबं�धत अ�ध�नयम क� धारा 3 और 4 \nके अंतगर्त रे ल सम्पित्त क� चोर� और दुरु�व�नयोग के �कसी अपराध से संबं�धत षडयंत्र के अपराध क� \nप�र�ध का �वस्तार करने हेतु य