r had just gone for that. Now he has come. \nAfter this, he will, move the Motion. Then we will take up Special \nMentions and then the House will be adjourned...(Interruptions)... I will \ntell you about the Motion. It is a small Bill, Let the Bill be passed. \nPlease cooperate. He is the last speaker. \n\n 236 \nश्री सैयद अज़ीज़ पाशा (आंध्र प्रदे श): सर, म� अपनी बात दो �मनट के अंदर समाप्त कर दूंगा। \nइस �बल के बारे म� मेरे mixed reactions ह �, इनम� कु छ अ च् छे points ह� और कु छ खराब \npoints भी ह�। इसम� जो nominated posts रखे गए ह�, वे भी subtle ways से रखे गए ह� �क \nकै स े इस पर क ं ट्रोल करना है और डेमोक्र े सी को कै स े  subvert करना है। म� इ स के हक म� नह�ं हूं �क \nइसम� nominated members को रखा जाए। \n\n 237 \nसर, दूसर� बात यह है �क NDMC क� जो revenue है. वह MCD से दोगुनी है। Revenue तो \nदोगुनी है, ले�कन सु�वधाएं दोगुनी नह�ं है। अगर हम NDMC  areas म� law and order \nsituation को दे ख�गे या basic सु�वधाओं क� िस्थ�त दे ख�गे, तो बड़ा ताज्जुब होगा। जब म�ने कु छ \nलोग� से contact �कया, तो मुझे यह सुन कर ताज्जुब हुआ �क NDMC areas के कई इलाक� म� \nपानी क� सु�वधाएं और अन्य कई �कस्म क� सु�वधाएं भी नह�ं है। \nइ स के �लए संबं�धत �ेत्र के लोग बहुत \nपरे शान ह�। अगर हम NDMC इ ल ा के के law and order से संबं�धत आंकड़े दे ख�, तो पता चलेगा �क \nइस इ ल ा के म� ज्यादा वारदात होती ह�। हम� यह सोचना चा�हए �क इन सभी मुद्द� को कै स े हल �कया \nजाए? \nसर, मेरा अं�तम point यह है �क �दल्ल� म� पटर� पर रहने वाले बहुत से गर�ब लोग ह�, उनसे \nआप पैसा तो वसूल करते है, ले�कन पैसा वसूल करने के बाद उनको वहां से �नकाल बाहर करते ह�। यह \nबात गलत है। गर�ब लोग� को भी जीने का हक रहना चा�हए और pavement dwellers के हक को \nभी हम� उनसे नह�ं छ�नना चा�हए। \nइसम� unauthorised colonies के बारे म� भी बात कह� गई है। Unauthorised colony \nकै स े बनती है? लैण्ड मा�फया कै स े काम करते ह�? िजस वक्त इसक� पूर� प्ला�नंग होती है या प्लॉ�टंग \nहोती है, उस समय संबं�धत अ�धकार� खामोश रहते ह�, क्य��क वह भी उसम� collude करते ह�। जब \nपानी सर से ऊपर आता है, तब वहां पर demolition क� बात आती है और unauthorised \ncolonies क� बात आती है। म� 25-30 साल पहले क�  standing commitee का resolution \nबताना चाहता हूं �क अगर �कसी पर एक्शन लेना है, तो इिब्तदा उस पर एक्शन ल�। जब यह कालोनी \nबन जाती है, उ स के बाद demolition होगा, तो उसको untold misery या suffering कह�गे। \nयह बात ठ�क नह�ं है। ताज्जुब क� बात यह है �क NDMC म� कोई town palnner नह�ं है। अगर \ntown planning वाले ह�गे, तो इन तमाम चीज� को दे ख सकते ह�। म� इतना ह� कहते हुए अपनी \nबात समाप्त करता हूं �क इसम� जो खा�मयां ह�, अगर उनको दूर कर द�गे, तो अच्छा रहेगा। धन्यवाद। \nMR. DEPUTY CHAIRMAN: Now, the hon. Minister to reply.  \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS (SHRI \nMULLAPPALLY RAMACHANDRAN): Mr. Deputy Chairman, Sir, at the outset, let \nme thank the four hon. Members who have taken part in the discussion. I \nhave taken note of the valuable suggestions and observations made by each \nMember and I once again thank them. \nSir, the New Delhi Municipal Council (Amendment) Bill, 2011 is a very \nsmall piece of legislation. That is initiated wholly due to the \nexigencies created by the delimitation of Assembly constituencies in \nDelhi. As I mentioned in my opening remarks, in the delimitation, the \n\n 238 \nnumber of Assembly constituencies falling  wholly or partly in the New \nDelhi area have been reduced from three to two. This necessitated \ncorresponding changes in the New Delhi Municipal Council Act, 1994 which  \n\n 239 \nprovides for three MLAs of the area to be made members of the Council. \nSecondly, Sir, the Government has decided to accept the recommendations \nof the Estimates Committee of the 14th Lok Sabha to make Member of \nParliament of the area as a member of the Council with voting rights. \nEarlier, he was only a special invitee. \nSir, the third change which we have suggested is to increase the \nnumber of members nominated to the Council from various fields from two \nto four to have wider representation in the Council. It will also give \nthe Government of Delhi more say in the affairs of the Council. Sir, the \nlast change that we have suggested in the composition of the Council is \nto increase the SC representation from one to two. This wouJd empower the \nweaker sections of the society vis-a-vis the functioning of the Council. \nSir, while considering all these changes in the composition of the \nCouncil, it has been felt that the meetings of the Council should be \nchaired in such a manner so as to ensure people’s representation in \nproper perspective and spirit. For this purpose, it is proposed to change \nthe order of the members chairing the meeting of the Council. Now, the \nChief Minister of Delhi or the Minister of the Central Government or the \nMinister of the Delhi Government or the MP of that area will chair the \nmeeting in that order, if he or she attends the meeting, ahead of the \nChairperson of the Council who is an officer of the level of Joint \nSecretary to the Government of India. \nSir, a very important point has been raised by the hon. first \nspeaker, Mr. Avinash Rai Khanna, about the democratic spirit of the \nCouncil. Sir, on this particular aspect, I have an important point to \nsuggest. The questions whether NDMC should be an elected body, whether \nthere should be full State, etc. can be considered separately, We will \ncall all political parties in Delhi and consider these issues separately. \nFor the present, in order to reflect the changed circumstances, let us \nplease pass this Bill. \nश्री नरे न्द्र कु मार कश्यप : मान्यवर, एक स्पष्ट�करण नह�ं आया है। म�ने यह अनुरोध �कया था \n�क जब आपने म�हलाओं को तीन सीट� द�ं ह�, एससी को दो सीट� द� ह�, तो बैकवडर् को 27 परस�ट \n�रज़व�शन दे ने म� आपको क्या आपित्त है? अगर आप उसम� यह व्यवस्था कर द�, तो क्या परे शानी \nआएगी? कृ पया मंत्री जी बताएँ। \nSHRI MULLAPPALLY RAMACHANDRAN: Sir, at  the moment, there is only one \nrepresentative belonging to SC category. Now, it has been increased to \n\n 240 \ntwo. \nMR. DEPUTY CHAIRMAN: He is talking about backward communities. \nSHRI MULLAPPALLY RAMACHANDRAN: Sir, at the important points raised by \nhon. Members will receive the attention of the Government. Thank you, \nSir. \n\n 241 \nMR. DEPUTY CHAIRMAN: Now, the question is: \nThat the Bill further to amend the New Delhi Municipal Council Act, \n1994, as passed by Lok Sabha, be taken into consideration. \n The motion was adopted. \nMR. DEPUTY CHAIRMAN: Now, we shall take up Clause- by-Clause \nconsideration of the Bill. \nClauses 2 and 3 were added to the Bill.  \nClause 1, the Enacting Formula and the Title were added to the Bill. \nSHRI MULLAPALLY RAMACHANDRAN: I beg to move : \nThat the Bill be passed.  \nThe question was put and the motion was adopted. \n________ \nMOTION FOR CONSTITUTION OF A JOINT COMMITTEE FOR  \nWELFARE OF OTHER BACKWARD CLASSES (OBCs) \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF PARLIAMENTARY AFFAIRS (SHRI \nRAJEEV SHUKLA) : I move the following motion: \nThat this House concurs in the recommendation of the Lok Sabha that a \nCommittee of both the Houses to be called the ‘Committee for Welfare of \nOther Backward Classes (OBCs) be constituted for the purposes set out in \nthe motion adopted by the Lok Sabha at its sitting held on 21st December \n2011 and communicated to this House on that day, and reserves that this \nHouse do join in the said Committee and proceed to elect, in accordance \nwith the system of proportional  \nrepresentation by means of the single transferable vote, ten Members from \namongst the Members of this House to serve on the said Committee.” \nThe question was put and the motion was adopted.  \nMR DEPUTY CHAIRMAN: Now, Special Mentions. ..(Interruptions)… \nSHRI K.N. BALAGOPAL (Kerala) : I am on a point of order. I gave a \nnotice for statutory motion. I gave an amendment to the Papers Laid on \nthe Table about Major Airports Development Fee; and I gave it in the last \nsession. In the last session it was not listed. This session it has been \n\n 242 \nlisted. Even in today’s list it is there. But it is not be